  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Three different taps drip every $48$ seconds, $72$ seconds, and $108$ seconds, respectively. If they all drip at midday, then when do they next drip simultaneously?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "12:07:12 pm.\n\nThe next simultaneous drip is after $\\mathrm{LCM}(48,72,108)=432$ seconds, or 7 minutes 12 seconds.",
      "worked": "A simultaneous drip occurs after a common multiple of all three intervals; the next one occurs after their LCM.\n$$\\begin{align*}48&=2^4\\times3\\\\72&=2^3\\times3^2\\\\108&=2^2\\times3^3\\\\\\mathrm{LCM}(48,72,108)&=2^4\\times3^3\\\\\\mathrm{LCM}(48,72,108)&=432\\end{align*}$$\n$432$ seconds is $7$ minutes $12$ seconds, so the next simultaneous drip is at 12:07:12 pm.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 76
  },
